 "_doc": "Written by tag_measure.py (python3 -I tag_measure.py [STATE]). Frame F1 mm (+x forward, +y wearer's left, +z up). tag.* is the scanned snapback loop tag at the strap's wearer's-left end; its outer face's vertices and a planar (u across, v up) mm parameterisation centred on the face are in tag.outer_npz (u = (p - centre) . across, v = (p - centre) . up; across = up x normal points right as seen from behind). logo.rotate_deg is counter-clockwise positive as seen from behind (-90 = clockwise: the logo's top faces +u, its long side runs along v). logo.size_mm is the logo's tight bounding box on the face after the turn.",
 "note": "Brayden 2026-10-20: \"add our Reel48 logo onto the existing snapback tag ... on the left side of the velcro strap, there is already a little loop tag there ... put the attached logo vertically onto it. Should be a 90 degree turn for the logo to stack horizontally and look correct.\" Lead's decisions: turn clockwise as the No. 7 sample's REEL48 text (R48926-47.jpg), the tag follows the strap colour, the mark's colour contrasts automatically, the mark is fixed (not customer-editable), long side ~70 % of the face height with >= 1 mm to the side edges. Brayden 2026-10-21: \"Can you please make the Reel48 logo on the snapback tag slightly bigger? It should take up about 90% of the length of the tag and be centered on the rectangle.\" logo.size_rule frac_of_tag_length: long side 0.90 x the tag's height, short side long / aspect; 07_parts centres it on the production tag and gates side_margin_mm and centre_tol_mm there (the scanned face here is too narrow: logo.size_mm.side_clearance_mm).",
